091218.115: [09:12:18]              Specifies the protocol family to use. The protocol family identifier can be one of inet, inet6, bridge, mpls or link.  If this option is not present, the protocol family is guessed from other ar‐
091218.126: [09:12:18]       -f, -family <FAMILY>
091218.132: [09:12:18]
091218.150: [09:12:18]              Specify maximum number of loops the 'ip address flush' logic will attempt before giving up. The default is 10.  Zero (0) means loop until all addresses are removed.
091218.150: [09:12:18]       -l, -loops <COUNT>
091218.151: [09:12:18]
091218.161: [09:12:18]              Output more detailed information.
091218.168: [09:12:18]       -d, -details
091218.179: [09:12:18]
091218.186: [09:12:18]              Output more information. If the option appears twice or more, the amount of information increases.  As a rule, the information is statistics or some time values.
091218.198: [09:12:18]       -s, -stats, -statistics
091218.205: [09:12:18]
091218.206: [09:12:18]       -force Don't terminate ip on errors in batch mode.  If there were any errors during execution of the commands, the application return code will be non zero.
091218.219: [09:12:18]
091218.225: [09:12:18]              Read commands from provided file or standard input and invoke them.  First failure will cause termination of ip.
091218.225: [09:12:18]       -b, -batch <FILENAME>
091218.238: [09:12:18]
091218.245: [09:12:18]              output statistics with human readable values followed by suffix.
091218.259: [09:12:18]       -h, -human, -human-readable
091218.265: [09:12:18]
091218.265: [09:12:18]              Print the version of the ip utility and exit.
091218.284: [09:12:18]       -V, -Version
091218.284: [09:12:18]OPTIONS
091218.291: [09:12:18]
091218.298: [09:12:18]               -o[neline] | -rc[vbuf] [size] | -t[imestamp] | -ts[hort] | -n[etns] name | -N[umeric] | -a[ll] | -c[olor] | -br[ief] | -j[son] | -p[retty] }
091218.315: [09:12:18]       OPTIONS := { -V[ersion] | -h[uman-readable] | -s[tatistics] | -d[etails] | -r[esolve] | -iec | -f[amily] { inet | inet6 | link } | -4 | -6 | -I | -D | -B | -0 | -l[oops] { maximum-addr-flush-attempts } |
091218.322: [09:12:18]
091218.323: [09:12:18]       OBJECT := { link | address | addrlabel | route | rule | neigh | ntable | tunnel | tuntap | maddress | mroute | mrule | monitor | xfrm | netns | l2tp | tcp_metrics | token | macsec | vrf | mptcp }
091218.333: [09:12:18]
091218.341: [09:12:18]       ip [ -force ] -batch filename
091218.363: [09:12:18]
091218.371: [09:12:18]       ip [ OPTIONS ] OBJECT { COMMAND | help }
091218.391: [09:12:18]SYNOPSIS
091218.400: [09:12:18]
091218.710: [09:12:18]       ip - show / manipulate routing, network devices, interfaces and tunnels
091218.711: [09:12:18]NAME
091218.733: [09:12:18]
091218.749: [09:12:18]IP(8)                                                                                                  Linux                                                                                                 IP(8)
091221.108: [09:12:21]
091221.329: [09:12:21]       -a, -all
091221.411: [09:12:21]              executes specified command over all objects, it depends if command supports this option.
091221.473: [09:12:21]
091221.502: [09:12:21]       -c[color][={always|auto|never}
091221.539: [09:12:21]              Configure color output. If parameter is omitted or always, color output is enabled regardless of stdout state. If parameter is auto, stdout is checked to be a terminal before enabling color out‐
091221.579: [09:12:21]              put. If parameter is never, color output is disabled. If specified multiple times, the last one takes precedence. This flag is ignored if -json is also given.
091221.613: [09:12:21]
091221.640: [09:12:21]              Used color palette can be influenced by COLORFGBG environment variable (see ENVIRONMENT).
091221.673: [09:12:21]
091221.687: [09:12:21]       -t, -timestamp
091221.719: [09:12:21]              display current time when using monitor option.
091221.763: [09:12:21]
091221.804: [09:12:21]       -ts, -tshort
091221.845: [09:12:21]              Like -timestamp, but use shorter format.
091221.911: [09:12:21]
091222.100: [09:12:22]       -rc, -rcvbuf<SIZE>
091222.237: [09:12:22]              Set the netlink socket receive buffer size, defaults to 1MB.
091222.398: [09:12:22]
091222.501: [09:12:22]       -iec   print human readable rates in IEC units (e.g. 1Ki = 1024).
091222.577: [09:12:22]
091222.612: [09:12:22]       -br, -brief
091222.660: [09:12:22]              Print only basic information in a tabular format for better readability. This option is currently only supported by ip addr show and ip link show commands.
091222.702: [09:12:22]
091222.735: [09:12:22]       -j, -json
091222.766: [09:12:22]              Output results in JavaScript Object Notation (JSON).
091222.799: [09:12:22]
091222.846: [09:12:22]       -p, -pretty
091222.911: [09:12:22]              The default JSON format is compact and more efficient to parse but hard for most users to read.  This flag adds indentation for readability.
091223.154: [09:12:23]
091223.312: [09:12:23]IP - COMMAND SYNTAX
091223.563: [09:12:23]   OBJECT
091223.782: [09:12:23]       address
091223.859: [09:12:23]              - protocol (IP or IPv6) address on a device.
091223.939: [09:12:23]
091224.008: [09:12:24]       addrlabel
091224.120: [09:12:24]              - label configuration for protocol address selection.
091224.199: [09:12:24]
091224.346: [09:12:24]       l2tp   - tunnel ethernet over IP (L2TPv3).
091224.980: [09:12:24]
091225.064: [09:12:25]       link   - network device.
091225.325: [09:12:25]
091225.467: [09:12:25]       maddress
091226.237: [09:12:26]              - multicast address.
091226.299: [09:12:26]
091226.433: [09:12:26]       monitor
091227.093: [09:12:27]              - watch for netlink messages.
091227.167: [09:12:27]
091227.238: [09:12:27]       mptcp  - manage MPTCP path manager.
091227.376: [09:12:27]
091227.424: [09:12:27]       mroute - multicast routing cache entry.
091227.459: [09:12:27]
091227.523: [09:12:27]       mrule  - rule in multicast routing policy database.
091227.555: [09:12:27]
091227.583: [09:12:27]       neighbour
091227.621: [09:12:27]              - manage ARP or NDISC cache entries.
091227.652: [09:12:27]
091227.686: [09:12:27]       netns  - manage network namespaces.
091227.740: [09:12:27]
091227.786: [09:12:27]       ntable - manage the neighbor cache's operation.
091228.173: [09:12:28]
091228.384: [09:12:28]       route  - routing table entry.
091228.711: [09:12:28]
091228.845: [09:12:28]       rule   - rule in routing policy database.
091228.953: [09:12:28]
091229.050: [09:12:29]       tcp_metrics/tcpmetrics
091229.979: [09:12:29]              - manage TCP Metrics
091230.119: [09:12:30]
091230.195: [09:12:30]       token  - manage tokenized interface identifiers.
091230.223: [09:12:30]
091230.253: [09:12:30]       tunnel - tunnel over IP.
091230.280: [09:12:30]
091230.323: [09:12:30]       tuntap - manage TUN/TAP devices.
091230.344: [09:12:30]
091230.377: [09:12:30]       vrf    - manage virtual routing and forwarding devices.
091230.402: [09:12:30]
091230.428: [09:12:30]       xfrm   - manage IPSec policies.
091230.448: [09:12:30]
091230.481: [09:12:30]       The names of all objects may be written in full or abbreviated form, for example address can be abbreviated as addr or just a.
091230.502: [09:12:30]
091230.548: [09:12:30]   COMMAND
091230.578: [09:12:30]       Specifies the action to perform on the object.  The set of possible actions depends on the object type.  As a rule, it is possible to add, delete and show (or list ) objects, but some objects do not al‐
091230.621: [09:12:30]       low all of these operations or have some additional commands. The help command is available for all objects. It prints out a list of available commands and argument syntax conventions.
091230.678: [09:12:30]
091230.740: [09:12:30]       If no command is given, some default command is assumed.  Usually it is list or, if the objects of this class cannot be listed, help.
091230.876: [09:12:30]
091231.264: [09:12:31]ENVIRONMENT
091231.399: [09:12:31]       COLORFGBG
091231.593: [09:12:31]              If set, it's value is used for detection whether background is dark or light and use contrast colors for it.
091231.768: [09:12:31]
091231.852: [09:12:31]              COLORFGBG environment variable usually contains either two or three values separated by semicolons; we want the last value in either case.  If this value is 0-6 or 8, chose colors suitable for
091231.958: [09:12:31]              dark background:
091232.021: [09:12:32]
091232.153: [09:12:32]              COLORFGBG=";0" ip -c a
091232.501: [09:12:32]
091232.782: [09:12:32]EXIT STATUS
091233.110: [09:12:33]       Exit status is 0 if command was successful, and 1 if there is a syntax error.  If an error was reported by the kernel exit status is 2.
091233.173: [09:12:33]
091233.206: [09:12:33]EXAMPLES
091233.226: [09:12:33]       ip addr
091233.259: [09:12:33]           Shows addresses assigned to all network interfaces.
091233.294: [09:12:33]
091233.318: [09:12:33]       ip neigh
091233.347: [09:12:33]           Shows the current neighbour table in kernel.
091233.366: [09:12:33]
091233.374: [09:12:33]       ip link set x up
091233.392: [09:12:33]           Bring up interface x.
091233.419: [09:12:33]
091233.440: [09:12:33]       ip link set x down
091233.452: [09:12:33]           Bring down interface x.
091233.478: [09:12:33]
091233.518: [09:12:33]       ip route
091233.539: [09:12:33]           Show table routes.
091233.568: [09:12:33]
091233.611: [09:12:33]HISTORY
091233.654: [09:12:33]       ip was written by Alexey N. Kuznetsov and added in Linux 2.2.
091234.238: [09:12:34]
091234.439: [09:12:34]SEE ALSO
091234.639: [09:12:34]       ip-address(8), ip-addrlabel(8), ip-l2tp(8), ip-link(8), ip-maddress(8), ip-monitor(8), ip-mptcp(8), ip-mroute(8), ip-neighbour(8), ip-netns(8), ip-ntable(8), ip-route(8), ip-rule(8), ip-tcp_metrics(8),
091235.262: [09:12:35]       ip-token(8), ip-tunnel(8), ip-vrf(8), ip-xfrm(8)
091235.456: [09:12:35]       IP Command reference ip-cref.ps
091235.724: [09:12:35]
091236.069: [09:12:36]REPORTING BUGS
091236.260: [09:12:36]       Report any bugs to the Network Developers mailing list <netdev@vger.kernel.org> where the development and maintenance is primarily done.  You do not have to be subscribed to the list to send a message
091236.536: [09:12:36]       there.
091236.744: [09:12:36]
